=* postContent (string) – Current post content: {{ $('Fetch WordPress Post').first().json.content }}
* title (string) – Current post title: "{{ $('Fetch WordPress Post').first().json.title }}"
* feedback (string) – Editorial feedback to apply: {{ JSON.stringify($('Classify Comment Intent').first().json.message.content.feedback) }}
* image_id – New image URL if one was uploaded: {{ $('Upload New Image').isExecuted ? $('Upload New Image').first().json.url : null }}
* Optional constraints:
    * wordcount – Target total word count: {{ $('Fetch Task Details').first().json.data.notes.includes('REQUESTED WORD COUNT') ? $('Fetch Task Details').first().json.data.notes?.match(/REQUESTED WORD COUNT:\s*(\d+)/i)[1] : 1500 }}
    * sections – Target number of sections: {{ $('Fetch Task Details').first().json.data.notes.includes('REQUESTED SECTIONS') ? $('Fetch Task Details').first().json.data.notes?.match(/REQUESTED SECTIONS:\s*(\d+)/i)[1] : 6}}

Instructions:
1. Apply all feedback logically and naturally to postContent.
2. Ensure the final content meets the target wordcount and number of sections if provided.
3. Update the title only if feedback suggests it or the current title is unclear.
4. Preserve the original CTA if present.
5. Do not include the feedback summary in the output.
